{"title":"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Listing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Listing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Among the positive integers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, each of whose digits is a prime number, one is selected at random. What is the probability that the selected number is prime?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/205d103eb1630ac46b8455c9200d0b174c8d24e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\dfrac{8}{99}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\dfrac{2}{5}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\dfrac{9}{20}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)} \\dfrac{1}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\dfrac{9}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The one digit prime numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/92251f81dfcd78c67dd057d81543703f31419fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot4=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> ways to choose a two digit number with both digits as primes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose a one digit prime, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccd5ace955a316c131942306fda43d6abe43f7f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+16=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> ways. Out of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba318f7385187c693cb1859d9b4b1b587e649d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$53$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b03f8ead3b3da0bd2cbc1a41d8f01630e638f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are prime. Thus the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c09dfbd7ef1ae58ecaf2a5bf88cf2fa03adc7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{8}{20}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\dfrac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"99\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Listing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Listing)\">Solution 2 (Listing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Listing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the only primes digits are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it doesn't seem too hard to list all of the numbers out.\n</p>\n<ul><li>2- Prime;</li>\n<li>3- Prime;</li>\n<li>5- Prime;</li>\n<li>7- Prime;</li>\n<li>22- Composite;</li>\n<li>23- Prime;</li>\n<li>25- Composite;</li>\n<li>27- Composite;</li>\n<li>32- Composite;</li>\n<li>33- Composite;</li>\n<li>35- Composite;</li>\n<li>37- Prime;</li>\n<li>52- Composite;</li>\n<li>53- Prime;</li>\n<li>55- Composite;</li>\n<li>57- Composite;</li>\n<li>72- Composite;</li>\n<li>73- Prime;</li>\n<li>75- Composite;</li>\n<li>77- Composite.</li></ul>\n<p>Counting it out, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cases and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of these are prime. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c09dfbd7ef1ae58ecaf2a5bf88cf2fa03adc7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{8}{20}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\dfrac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"99\" height=\"48\" />.\n~JH. L\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RZDFs3qrw7Y\">https://youtu.be/RZDFs3qrw7Y</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/cL9wo9kcOGg\">https://youtu.be/cL9wo9kcOGg</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border